    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0208" n="158" xml:id="pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/5947</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-22T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1230. Your 2987, October 12, 5 p.m. Before action is taken on Webster’s message
                    to Red Cross, Department desires to know whether proposed relief requires
                    association with Bolshevik authorities. Department is of opinion that Bolshevik
                    regime has been preserved beyond its normal term by German support. Circular
                    telegram of September 20<anchor n="1" xml:id="d216-f1"/> asked all civilized
                    countries to protest against reign of terror which now prevails under Bolshevik
                    regime. Disastrous conditions at Petrograd are appreciated but other
                    considerations must now also be considered. Please answer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
